// A funded vending machine: reactions that are not paid for do not fire.
//
// Cost-profile surface:
//   {P}sig                 a process P signed by `sig`
//   purse c {s : ()}       a purse on channel c holding one token signed `s`
//   purse c {s : s : ()}   the same purse with two stacked tokens
//   purse c {()}           an empty purse on channel c
//
// A sale is a COMM between a machine receive and a customer send.  The
// funding rule is located: the sale consumes one token per endpoint
// signature -- here machine * customer -- and those tokens must be found
// in purses sitting on the `vend` channel itself.  There is no ambient
// bank account.
//
// The till holds two `machine` tokens; alice has a coin in the channel
// purse; bob has none.  Exactly one sale fires (alice's).  Bob's order is
// left facing a live machine endpoint and a till that could pay the
// machine's own share: an unfunded reaction is disabled, not slowed.
//
// Run: ./cetta --lang rhocalc --profile cost examples/rho/cost/vending_machine.rho

{for ($order <- vend) {{0}served}}machine
| {for ($order <- vend) {{0}served}}machine
| {vend!({0}coin)}alice
| {vend!({0}coin)}bob
| purse vend {machine : machine : ()}
| purse vend {alice : ()}
